{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Bimanual Interaction.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Bimanual Interaction.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"bimanual interaction bimanual interaction","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Bimanual Interaction.md","fileName":"Bimanual Interaction.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Bimanual Interaction","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 13:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Spatial Interaction]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Spatial Interaction","3D Manipulation","Progressive Refinement","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Bimanual Interaction.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Bimanual Interaction.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"bimanual interaction bimanual interaction","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Bimanual Interaction.md","fileName":"Bimanual Interaction.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Bimanual Interaction","heading":"Bimanual Interaction","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Bimanual interaction coordinates both hands to perform a task. It may use two devices, two tracked hands, or different controls assigned to each hand.\n\nSymmetric interaction gives both hands similar roles; asymmetric interaction gives them different but coordinated roles. Timing can also be synchronous or asynchronous. For example, one hand may establish a frame or region while the other performs a more precise action inside it.\n\nBimanual design can support integrated [[3D Manipulation]] and [[Progressive Refinement]], but the mapping should respect hand roles, device ergonomics, and the flow between actions rather than merely duplicating controls.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Spatial Interaction","3D Manipulation","Progressive Refinement","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pa